      "problem": "$|-\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}|=$",
      "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|-a|=|a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n|\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}| & = \\\\ \\frac{|2{k}^{2}|}{|3|} & = \\\\ \\frac{|2|\\cdot |{k}^{2}|}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{2|{k}^{2}|}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${k}^{2}\\ge 0$ for any real $k,$ we have that $|{k}^{2}|={k}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2|{k}^{2}|}{3} & =\\frac{2{k}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
